From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:08:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 255/342] app_server: emoji sequences drawn as one emoji

Flags (two regional indicators), ZWJ sequences (a family, a
profession), skin tones, keycaps and tag sequences (England's flag)
were drawn a character at a time: two letters in boxes, three people,
a hand and a colour swatch. The colour emoji font has a ligature for
each in its GSUB table (the 'ccmp' feature, 3888 of them in Noto Color
Emoji); the app_server has no shaper.

EmojiSequences reads the colour font's cmap and GSUB once, from the
font file, and applies the ligature lookups of 'ccmp' as a shaper
would (each lookup over all the glyphs in turn, variation selectors
left out: the font has no glyph for them). The glyph layout looks for a
sequence only after a character that something joins (U+200D and what
follows it, a skin tone, U+20E3, tags, a second regional indicator).
A sequence that becomes one ligature is drawn as that glyph of the
colour font, cached by its index (kGlyphCodeGlyphIndex); the sequence's
other characters get no width of their own. Without a colour font, or
without a ligature, the characters are drawn one at a time as before.
Shaping for other scripts would still need HarfBuzz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
